ined-builtin,\\n    58\\t   :builtin \\\"str_repeat\\\",\\n    59\\t   :oracle-expect \\\"ok\\\",\\n    60\\t   :engine-result\\n    61\\t   {:out \\\"\\\",\\n    62\\t    :diag [],\\n    63\\t    :uncaught\\n    64\\t    {:class \\\"Error\\\",\\n    65\\t     :message \\\"Call to undefined function str_repeat()\\\"}},\\n    66\\t   :engine-work-item \\\"Implement str_repeat().\\\"}\\n    67\\t  {:id \\\"Zend/tests/gc_012.phpt\\\",\\n    68\\t   :feature :gc-cycle-collection,\\n    69\\t   :builtin nil,\\n    70\\t   :oracle-expect \\\"int(0)\\\\nint(1000)\\\\nok\\\",\\n    71\\t   :engine-result\\n    72\\t   {:out \\\"\\\",\\n    73\\t    :diag [],\\n    74\\t    :uncaught\\n    75\\t    {:class \\\"Error\\\",\\n# Findings: PHPT manifest repair (p8 legacy retirement)\\n\\nSeat: the full e2e gate (`clojure -M:test -n yang.php.antlr.e2e-test`) was NOT run\\nhere per the HARD CONSTRAINT (laptop overload). EDN validity was verified locally\\n(`clojure.edn/read-string` round-trip, seconds). The shiva run is the deciding gate.\\n\\n## What changed (`test/yang/php/antlr/phpt_quick_mismatch_manifest.edn`, EDN round-trip)\\n\\n1. **bug64660 gap record**: the selection entry `Zend/tests/bug64660.phpt` carries\\n   `:expectf \\\"Parse error: memory exhausted in %s on line %d \\\"` and NO `:expect`\\n   (keys: `:id :path :slow :source :title :expectf`). The gap's `:oracle-expect`\\n   was `\\\"Okey\\\"` (stale — probably copied from bug63055's oracle). Set to `nil` so\\n   `(= (:expect entry) (:oracle-expect gap))` holds, and recorded the real oracle\\n   shape in a new `:oracle-expectf` key. `:engine-result {}` and the work-item\\n   text left untouched.\\n2. **bug63055 slow gap added** (8th record): entry `:expect \\\"okey\\\"`, `:slow true`,\\n   no `:needs`. Record: `:feature :undefined-builtin`, `:builtin \\\"str_replace\\\"`,\\n   `:oracle-expect \\\"okey\\\"`, `:engine-result {:out \\\"\\\" :diag [] :uncaught\\n   {:class \\\"Error\\\" :message \\\"Call to undefined function str_replace()\\\"}}`,\\n   `:engine-work-item \\\"Implement str_replace().\\\"` — mirroring the sibling\\n   str_repeat/serialize gap records. Engine result copied from the brief, NOT\\n   measured locally; shiva must confirm assertion `:568` (`engine-result` equality).\\n3. **Quick manifest regenerated from deltas**: removed 7 ids present in the\\n   manifest — `unset_cv08`, `bug69756`, `bug81705`, `bug67874`, `bug60350`,\\n   `bug45877`, `bug78502` — from `:known-gaps` entries AND `:descriptions`.\\n   New `:counts`: `zend-regression 61` (was a stale 70; the entries actually held\\n   67), `gc-cycle-collection 10`, `foreach-semantics 11`, `named-parameter-binding 3`,\\n   `unset-cv 3`, `array-reference 1`, `pass-by-reference 5`, `array-pointer 1`,\\n   `:total 95`, `:unsupported 57`. `:php-src-tag` stays `\\\"8.3.35\\\"`. All 7 slow\\n   records kept, plus the new bug63055 record.\\n\\n## Open items for the shiva pass\\n\\n- **Off-by-one vs the nightly note.** The brief's expected families are\\n  `{gc 10, foreach-by-ref 16, unset-cv 3, named-params 3, other 64}` (= 96), but\\n  this regeneration yields `other 63` / total 95. Of the brief's ~10 departed ids,\\n  3 (`bug71470`, `bug63206_1`, `bug79836_1`) were already absent from the manifest\\n  (removed by the earlier hand edit), leaving 7 real removals: 67-6=61 zend +\\n  array-ref + array-pointer = 63 other. If shiva reports `other 64` / total 96 or\\n  a different fail-id set, one id in this regeneration is wrong (suspect a\\n  `bug79836` vs `bug79836_1` mix-up — the manifest holds `bug79836.phpt`, the note\\n  names `bug79836_1`) or one more id needs removal; adjust `:known-gaps`,\\n  `:descriptions`, and `:counts` together on shiva.\\n- **Refusal count 58 -> 57** was taken from the brief, not measured. If shiva's\\n  quick run reports a different unsupported count, update `:unsupported` to match.\\n- **bug64660 `:engine-result {}`** was left as-is; if the shiva engine result for\\n  that OOM case is not `{}`, update the gap record to the measured value.\\n- **cljstyle/kondo**: neither binary is installed on this laptop and the repo has\\n  no lint config for `.edn` data files, so no lint gate was runnable here. The only\\n  touched file is the manifest (pure data, written by `pprint`).\\n- Caution: `clojure -M:test -e ...` triggers the test-runner main (it started\\n  \\\"Running tests\\\" here); it was killed immediately. Use `clojure -M -e` for EDN\\n  probes on this repo, never `-M:test` without `-n`.\\n# Findings: stale e2e pins on the MERGED branch (r2) — engine verified, pins updated\\n\\nDate: 2026-11-04. Branch: feat/p8-legacy-retirement @ 12e5eddc (includes origin/master P5/P7-a/P9).\\nNote: the predecessor's STOP verdict was correct for the pre-merge tree; on this merged tree all three\\npremises HOLD, so the pins were updated (commit `test(yang.php): ...` on this branch).\\n\\n## Verdict: all three items verified against the merged engine, fixtures updated\\n\\n1. **string-offset-write now works.** P9 commit `91c5c8cd` (\\\"feat(yang.php): P9 — the builtin surface\\n   slices\\\") deleted `php/str-write-error` and added `php/string-assign`, wired into `path-assign-at`\\n   (`src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc`). Focused walker probe:\\n   `<?php $s=\\\"ab\\\"; $s[0]=\\\"c\\\"; echo $s;` renders `\\\"cb\\\"`.\\n   - `test/yang/php/antlr/programs.cljc` `:string-offset-write` flipped from the G-str-offset-write\\n     refusal pin to the working expectation (`:out \\\"cb\\\"`, `:diag []`, `:uncaught`/`:gap` removed).\\n   - `test/yang/php/antlr/prelude_test.cljc` `array-path-assign-test` now pins\\n     `(php/echo (php/path-assign \\\"abc\\\" [0] \\\"x\\\"))` → `\\\"xbc\\\"`.\\n   - `docs/agents/known-gaps.md`: all 4 G-str-offset-write rows marked\\n     `closed 2026-11-04` citing `91c5c8cd`.\\n2. **strtoupper is a prelude builtin.** `builtins/supported` maps `\\\"strtoupper\\\"` to `php/bi-strtoupper`\\n   and `prelude/builtin-names` derives from that table, so no `:yang.php/unknown-builtin` warning is\\n   emitted and the call runs. `e2e_test.clj` `lowering-warnings-test` updated to no-warning + `\\\"A\\\"`.\\n3. **`$$a[0] = 1` now assigns through.** `base-location` (`lower.cljc`) locates a `Dollar`+`VarName`\\n   base as `{:var {:dynamic-name ...}}`, and `write-loc` writes a dynamic var with a path back via\\n   `dict-put!`. Focused walker probes: `<?php $$a[0] = 1;` lowers with no diagnostics (renders `\\\"\\\"`);\\n   `<?php $a = \\\"x\\\"; $x = [10, 20]; $$a[0] = 1; echo $x[0]; echo \\\",\\\"; echo $x[1];` renders `\\\"1,20\\\"`;\\n   `<?php $a = \\\"y\\\"; $$a[0] = 1; echo $y[0];` renders `\\\"1\\\"` (vivifies). So the engine resolves it as\\n   `${$a}[0]`. Refusals entry removed; new `variable-variable-offset-assign-test` pins `\\\"1,20\\\"`.\\n\\n## Laptop gates (all green)\\n\\n- `clojure -M:test -v yang.php.antlr.e2e-test/fixtures-on-the-walker-test\\n  -v .../lowering-warnings-test -v .../refusals-are-named-test\\n  -v .../variable-variable-offset-assign-test` → 4 tests, 557 assertions, 0 failures.\\n- `clojure -M:test -n yang.php.antlr.prelude-test` → 33 tests, 373 assertions, 0 failures.\\n- `clojure -M:kondo --lint` over the three touched test files → 0 errors, 0 warnings.\\n- No cljstyle runner is configured in this repo (`.cljstyle` present, no alias/CI invocation); edits\\n  match surrounding formatting. Full `e2e-test` namespace NOT run locally per the hard constraint.\\n\\n## Oracle: NOT performed on laptop (no docker/php) — seat oracle-check list for shiva\\n\\nPHP-truth assumed from the unambiguous documented behavior; the seat must confirm each on `php:8.3`\\nbefore landing (mark any doubt — none structural, but all three are oracle-unconfirmed):\\n\\n1. `php -r '$s=\\\"ab\\\"; $s[0]=\\\"c\\\"; echo $s;'` must print `cb`.\\n2. `php -r 'echo strtoupper(\\\"a\\\");'` must print `A`.\\n3. `php -r '$a = \\\"x\\\"; $x = [10, 20]; $$a[0] = 1; echo $x[0], \\\",\\\", $x[1];'` — engine prints `1,20`\\n   (i.e. `${$a}[0]` resolution); confirm Zend agrees, else the new pin's reading is wrong.\\n4. Seat gate: full `clojure -M:test -n yang.php.antlr.e2e-test` on shiva (includes the slow\\n   `fixtures-on-every-vm-test`, not run here).\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_21\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba src/dev/yang/php/oracle.clj | sed -n '1,165p'; nl -ba test/yang/php/antlr/request_context_test.clj | head -100; rg -n 'bind-request|request-array|merge-loop|bi-ob-end|headers already' src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc; cat collab/orch-lane/*request* 2>/dev/null\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_21\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba src/dev/yang/php/oracle.clj | sed -n '1,165p'; nl -ba test/yang/php/antlr/request_context_test.clj | head -100; rg -n 'bind-request|request-array|merge-loop|bi-ob-end|headers already' src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc; cat collab/orch-lane/*request* 2>/dev/null\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\t(ns yang.php.oracle\\n     2\\t  \\\"PHP 8.3 CLI oracle runner for `yang.php.antlr.programs`\\n     3\\t   (docs/design/yang.php.md sections 14, 17.3).\\n     4\\t\\n     5\\t   For every fixture in `programs/fixtures` (plus `matrix-source` and\\n     6\\t   `float-cases`), writes the PHP source to a temporary file and runs:\\n     7\\t     docker run --rm -v <dir>:/w -w /w php:8.3-cli php \\\\\\\\\\n     8\\t       -d display_errors=1 -d html_errors=0 -d error_reporting=E_ALL \\\\\\\\\\n     9\\t       -d log_errors=0 <file>\\n    10\\t   Parses stdout into `:out`, `:diag` (`[[errno message] ...]`) and `:uncaught`\\n    11\\t   (`{:class c :message m}`), and compares against each fixture's expectation\\n    12\\t   (or `:departure/:zend` for departure fixtures).\\\"\\n    13\\t  (:require\\n    14\\t    [clojure.java.io :as io]\\n    15\\t    [clojure.java.shell :as sh]\\n    16\\t    [clojure.string :as str]\\n    17\\t    [yang.php.antlr.programs :as programs]\\n    18\\t    [yang.php.antlr.programs-p3b :as p3b]\\n    19\\t    [yang.php.antlr.programs-p4 :as p4]\\n    20\\t    [yang.php.antlr.programs-p5 :as p5]\\n    21\\t    [yang.php.antlr.programs-p6 :as p6])\\n    22\\t  (:import\\n    23\\t    (java.nio.charset\\n    24\\t      StandardCharsets)\\n    25\\t    (java.nio.file\\n    26\\t      Files)\\n    27\\t    (java.nio.file.attribute\\n    28\\t      FileAttribute)))\\n    29\\t\\n    30\\t\\n    31\\t(def banner\\n    32\\t  \\\"The pinned PHP 8.3 CLI oracle provenance banner.\\\"\\n    33\\t  p3b/banner)\\n    34\\t\\n    35\\t\\n    36\\t(def ^:private errno-of\\n    37\\t  {\\\"Warning\\\" 2,\\n    38\\t   \\\"Notice\\\" 8,\\n    39\\t   \\\"Deprecated\\\" 8192,\\n    40\\t   \\\"Fatal error\\\" 1})\\n    41\\t\\n    42\\t\\n    43\\t(defn- location-pattern\\n    44\\t  \\\"The regex source of a PHP source location below `/w/`: the entry `file`\\n    45\\t   itself, or, for a multi-unit fixture run in `/w/<unit-dir>`, any unit file\\n    46\\t   below the directory.\\\"\\n    47\\t  [file unit-dir]\\n    48\\t  (if unit-dir\\n    49\\t    (str (java.util.regex.Pattern/quote unit-dir) \\\"/[^\\\\\\\\s:]+\\\")\\n    50\\t    (java.util.regex.Pattern/quote file)))\\n    51\\t\\n    52\\t\\n    53\\t(defn- strip-location\\n    54\\t  ([s file] (strip-location s file nil))\\n    55\\t  ([s file unit-dir]\\n    56\\t   (str/replace s\\n    57\\t                (re-pattern (str \\\" in /w/\\\" (location-pattern file unit-dir) \\\" on line \\\\\\\\d+\\\"))\\n    58\\t                \\\"\\\")))\\n    59\\t\\n    60\\t\\n    61\\t(defn parse-stdout\\n    62\\t  \\\"Parse PHP CLI stdout for `/w/<file>` into\\n    63\\t   `{:out <string> :diag [[errno msg] ...] :uncaught {:class c :message m}-or-nil}`.\\n    64\\t   With `unit-dir`, locations in any file below `/w/<unit-dir>` are stripped\\n    65\\t   (a multi-unit fixture).\\\"\\n    66\\t  ([raw file] (parse-stdout raw file nil))\\n    67\\t  ([raw file unit-dir]\\n    68\\t   (let [qfile (location-pattern file unit-dir)\\n    69\\t         strip-location (fn [s file] (strip-location s file unit-dir))\\n    70\\t         ;; The uncaught block ends at PHP's own terminator, so output written\\n    71\\t         ;; after it (shutdown functions, destructors) stays in :out.\\n    72\\t         uncaught-re (re-pattern\\n    73\\t                       (str \\\"(?s)\\\\\\\\nFatal error: Uncaught ([^:]+): ([^\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n]*) in /w/\\\"\\n    74\\t                            qfile\\n    75\\t                            \\\":\\\\\\\\d+\\\\\\\\nStack trace:\\\\\\\\n.*?\\\\\\\\n  thrown in /w/\\\"\\n    76\\t                            qfile\\n    77\\t                            \\\" on line \\\\\\\\d+\\\\\\\\n\\\"))\\n    78\\t         fatal-re (re-pattern\\n    79\\t                    (str \\\"\\\\\\\\nFatal error: ([^\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n]*) in /w/\\\"\\n    80\\t                         qfile\\n    81\\t                         \\\" on line \\\\\\\\d+\\\\\\\\n\\\"))\\n    82\\t         diag-re (re-pattern\\n    83\\t                   (str \\\"\\\\\\\\n(Warning|Notice|Deprecated): ([^\\\\\\\\r\\\\\\\\n]*?) in /w/\\\"\\n    84\\t                        qfile\\n    85\\t                        \\\" on line \\\\\\\\d+\\\\\\\\n\\\"))\\n    86\\t         [without-fatal uncaught]\\n    87\\t         (if-let [[_ cls msg] (re-find uncaught-re raw)]\\n    88\\t           [(str/replace raw uncaught-re \\\"\\\")\\n    89\\t            {:class cls, :message (strip-location msg file)}]\\n    90\\t           (if-let [[_ msg] (re-find fatal-re raw)]\\n    91\\t             [(str/replace raw fatal-re \\\"\\\")\\n    92\\t              {:class \\\"Error\\\", :message (strip-location msg file)}]\\n    93\\t             [raw nil]))\\n    94\\t         diags (volatile! [])\\n    95\\t         out (str/replace without-fatal\\n    96\\t                          diag-re\\n    97\\t                          (fn [[_ kind msg]]\\n    98\\t                            (vswap! diags conj [(get errno-of kind) (strip-location msg file)])\\n    99\\t                            \\\"\\\"))]\\n   100\\t     {:out out,\\n   101\\t      :diag @diags,\\n   102\\t      :uncaught uncaught})))\\n   103\\t\\n   104\\t\\n   105\\t(defn run-php-file\\n   106\\t  \\\"Run `<file>` inside `<dir>` via Docker `php:8.3-cli` and return the parsed\\n   107\\t   `{:out :diag :uncaught :exit}`. With `unit-dir`, the working directory is\\n   108\\t   `/w/<unit-dir>` and `file` is relative to it (a multi-unit fixture).\\\"\\n   109\\t  ([dir file] (run-php-file dir file nil))\\n   110\\t  ([dir file unit-dir]\\n   111\\t   (let [{:keys [out err exit]}\\n   112\\t         (sh/sh \\\"docker\\\" \\\"run\\\" \\\"--rm\\\"\\n   113\\t                \\\"-v\\\" (str (.toAbsolutePath (.toPath (io/file dir))) \\\":/w\\\")\\n   114\\t                \\\"-w\\\" (if unit-dir (str \\\"/w/\\\" unit-dir) \\\"/w\\\")\\n   115\\t                \\\"php:8.3-cli\\\" \\\"php\\\"\\n   116\\t                \\\"-d\\\" \\\"display_errors=1\\\"\\n   117\\t                \\\"-d\\\" \\\"html_errors=0\\\"\\n   118\\t                \\\"-d\\\" \\\"error_reporting=E_ALL\\\"\\n   119\\t                \\\"-d\\\" \\\"log_errors=0\\\"\\n   120\\t                file\\n   121\\t                :out-enc \\\"UTF-8\\\")]\\n   122\\t     (assoc (parse-stdout out (if unit-dir (str unit-dir \\\"/\\\" file) file) unit-dir)\\n   123\\t            :err err\\n   124\\t            :exit exit))))\\n   125\\t\\n   126\\t\\n   127\\t(defn- write-source!\\n   128\\t  [dir file ^String source]\\n   129\\t  (Files/write (.toPath (io/file dir file))\\n   130\\t               (.getBytes source StandardCharsets/UTF_8)\\n   131\\t               (make-array java.nio.file.OpenOption 0)))\\n   132\\t\\n   133\\t\\n   134\\t(defn- unit-actual\\n   135\\t  \\\"Run the multi-unit `fixture`: every unit is written below `<dir>/<id>/`,\\n   136\\t   `main.php` is run with that directory as the working directory, and\\n   137\\t   `/w/<id>` is replaced by `.` in everything the program printed (the\\n   138\\t   comparison's definition, plan P6 2.5 rule 2; corner C37).\\\"\\n   139\\t  [dir {:keys [id units main], :or {main \\\"main.php\\\"}}]\\n   140\\t  (let [unit-dir (name id)\\n   141\\t        norm (fn [s] (str/replace s (str \\\"/w/\\\" unit-dir) \\\".\\\"))]\\n   142\\t    (doseq [[path source] units]\\n   143\\t      (let [f (io/file dir unit-dir path)]\\n   144\\t        (io/make-parents f)\\n   145\\t        (write-source! dir (str unit-dir \\\"/\\\" path) source)))\\n   146\\t    (let [actual (run-php-file dir main unit-dir)]\\n   147\\t      (-> actual\\n   148\\t          (update :out norm)\\n   149\\t          (update :diag (fn [ds] (mapv (fn [[errno msg]] [errno (norm msg)]) ds)))\\n   150\\t          (update :uncaught #(some-> % (update :message norm)))))))\\n   151\\t\\n   152\\t\\n   153\\t(defn check-fixture\\n   154\\t  \\\"Run `fixture` in temporary directory `dir` and return a check record.\\\"\\n   155\\t  [dir {:keys [id source units out diag uncaught departure gap oracle], :as fixture}]\\n   156\\t  (let [file (str (name id) \\\".php\\\")]\\n   157\\t    (when-not units (write-source! dir file source))\\n   158\\t    (let [actual (if units (unit-actual dir fixture) (run-php-file dir file))\\n   159\\t          expected-out (cond departure (:zend departure)\\n   160\\t                             gap \\\"\\\"\\n   161\\t                             :else out)\\n   162\\t          expected-diag (vec (cond departure (:zend-diag departure)\\n   163\\t                                   gap []\\n   164\\t                                   :else (or diag [])))\\n   165\\t          expected-uncaught (cond departure (:zend-uncaught departure)\\n     1\\t(ns yang.php.antlr.request-context-test\\n     2\\t  \\\"P5 request records, response records, output buffering and isolation.\\\"\\n     3\\t  (:require\\n     4\\t    [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\\n     5\\t    [yang.php.antlr.e2e-harness :as h]\\n     6\\t    [yang.php.antlr.programs-p5 :as p5]))\\n     7\\t\\n     8\\t\\n     9\\t(defn- diagnostics\\n    10\\t  [r]\\n    11\\t  (mapv (juxt :errno :message) (:php/diag r)))\\n    12\\t\\n    13\\t\\n    14\\t(deftest request-binding-smoke-test\\n    15\\t  (is (= \\\"1\\\" (:php/out (h/run-raw \\\"<?php echo 1;\\\" {})))))\\n    16\\t\\n    17\\t\\n    18\\t(deftest request-context-fixtures-test\\n    19\\t  (doseq [{:keys [id source request out diag response status]} p5/fixtures]\\n    20\\t    (testing (name id)\\n    21\\t      (let [r (h/run-raw source request)]\\n    22\\t        (is (= out (:php/out r)))\\n    23\\t        (is (= (vec diag) (diagnostics r)))\\n    24\\t        (when response (is (= response (:php/response r))))\\n    25\\t        (when status (is (= status (:php/status r))))\\n    26\\t        (is (nil? (:php/uncaught r)))))))\\n    27\\t\\n    28\\t\\n    29\\t(deftest requests-in-separate-tasks-share-nothing-test\\n    30\\t  (let [source (str \\\"<?php header('X-Request: ' . $_GET['value']);\\\"\\n    31\\t                    \\\" echo $_GET['value']; $_GET['value'] = 'changed';\\\")\\n    32\\t        request-a (assoc p5/request :php.request/query (p5/request-array [[\\\"value\\\" \\\"A\\\"]]))\\n    33\\t        request-b (assoc p5/request :php.request/query (p5/request-array [[\\\"value\\\" \\\"B\\\"]]))\\n    34\\t        a (h/run-raw source request-a)\\n    35\\t        b (h/run-raw source request-b)]\\n    36\\t    (is (= \\\"A\\\" (:php/out a)))\\n    37\\t    (is (= \\\"B\\\" (:php/out b)))\\n    38\\t    (is (= [{:php.response/header \\\"X-Request: A\\\", :replace true}\\n    39\\t            {:php.response/body \\\"A\\\"}]\\n    40\\t           (:php/response a)))\\n    41\\t    (is (= [{:php.response/header \\\"X-Request: B\\\", :replace true}\\n    42\\t            {:php.response/body \\\"B\\\"}]\\n    43\\t           (:php/response b)))\\n    44\\t    (is (empty? (:php/diag a)))\\n    45\\t    (is (empty? (:php/diag b)))))\\n328:    [php/request-array-loop\\n332:           (php/request-array-loop entries (+ i 1)\\n335:    [php/request-array\\n341:           (php/request-array-loop entries 0 (php/empty-array)))))]\\n344:       (php/request-array (get request field)))]\\n345:    [php/bind-request!\\n359:             req (php/merge-loop (php/vconj (php/vconj [] geta) post)\\n390:    [php/bi-ob-end-clean\\n399:         (if (= s false) false (do (php/bi-ob-end-clean args) s))))]\\n400:    [php/bi-ob-end-flush\\n403:         (if (= s false) false (do (php/bi-ob-end-clean args) (php/echo s) true))))]\\n407:         (do (php/warn 2 \\\"Cannot modify header information - headers already sent\\\") true)\\n4836:    [php/merge-loop\\n4841:             (php/merge-loop args (+ i 1) n (php/spread-loop acc v 0 (php/array-count v)))\\n4848:     (fn [args] (php/merge-loop args 0 (data/count args) (php/empty-array)))]\\n# P5 request context findings\\n\\n## Delivered\\n\\n- Bound `$_GET`, `$_POST`, `$_COOKIE`, `$_SERVER`, `$_ENV`, `$_FILES`, and `$_REQUEST` from an explicit, task-local request record. Request collections accept either PHP arrays or ordered entry vectors; missing collections become empty arrays. `$_REQUEST` uses GET-then-POST replacement order.\\n- Added output-buffer stack operations, ordered response records for headers/cookies/status/body, and headers-after-output diagnostics.\\n- Lowered both `exit`/`die` parser forms to the runtime exit path. Exit runs shutdown functions, returns its status, and is not reported as an uncaught error.\\n- Added user error triggering, handler restoration, `getenv`, and `php_sapi_name` registrations.\\n- Added eight hand-derived P5 fixtures, all marked `:oracle :pending`, plus an independent-task isolation test using two separate VM sessions.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- `clojure -M:test -n yang.php.antlr.request-context-test`: 3 tests, 35 assertions, all passing.\\n- `clojure -M:test -n yang.php.antlr.class-model-test -n yang.php.antlr.objects-test -n yang.php.antlr.generators-test`: 14 tests, 1201 assertions, all passing.\\n- `clojure -M:kondo --lint` over all changed Clojure files: 0 errors, 0 warnings.\\n- Managed `cljstyle 0.17.642` check over all changed Clojure files: passing.\\n- `git diff --check`: passing.\\n\\nNo PHP oracle recording was performed, as requested for this round. No push was performed.\\n{\\\"role\\\":\\\"meta\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"system.version\\\",\\\"version\\\":\\\"2.4.0\\\"}\\n{\\\"role\\\":\\\"assistant\\\",\\\"tool_calls\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"function\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"tool_mxx5OnuwUhFjOGUiuNe2aG5H\\\",\\\"function\\\":{\\\"name\\\":\\\"Read\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":\\\"{\\\\\\\"path\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/tmp/kimi-p5.md\\\\\\\"}\\\"}}]}\\n{\\\"role\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool_call_id\\\":\\\"tool_mxx5OnuwUhFjOGUiuNe2aG5H\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"1\\\\tCreated-Local: 2026-11-03 1x:xx +0700\\\\n2\\\\tCoding-Agent: kimi\\\\n3\\\\tSession: fresh (engineer round — P5)\\\\n4\\\\tWorktree: /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p5 (branch feat/p5-request-context @ origin/master, 6e587996)\\\\n5\\\\t\\\\n6\\\\t# Task: P5 — request context (yang.php.md section 15, the P5 row)\\\\n7\\\\t\\\\n8\\\\tScope: `$_*` superglobals from the request record; `ob_*` output buffering; headers, cookies and status as response records; `exit`; the error handler; the warnings stream.\\\\n9\\\\t\\\\n10\\\\tAcceptance (the P5 row): superglobals reproducible from a fixture record (exit criterion 3); the headers-after-output warning; two requests in two tasks share nothing (exit criterion 5).\\\\n11\\\\t\\\\n12\\\\tMethod, per the track's standing pattern:\\\\n13\\\\t1. Read section 15's P5 row, the request-record model in yang.php.md, and the existing prelude/fixture structure (programs_p4.cljc's fx pat