p.\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md:583:M4 shall replace `:yin.safepoint/reasons` with\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md:584:`:yin.safepoint/kinds`, whose values are static possibilities from\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md:596:a naming correction to the Phase 1 safepoint API, not a new `v2`\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md:597:execution revision: `:yin.safepoint/reasons` was not a component named\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md:602:The lift driver must check the pc against the static safepoint set,\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md:622:UCF 7.11's safepoint harness must run each 7.4.1 row, including both\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md:655:Second, the `\\\\\\\"v3\\\\\\\"` canonicalizer and the stack-shaped safepoint halves\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md:659:safepoint facts and frame validator live in `yin.vm.semantic.code`,\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md:832:**I-9 — 2026-10-16, any-PC.** The current lift rejects active control and queued completed outcomes, while the holder runs unrestricted computation. Slices 6d-a, 6d-b and 6e extend the carrier to run states and complete scheduler products. 6d-a includes completed stream/FFI/link/install outcomes, cursor-update encoding, bounded bridge-aware fuel and closed-gate execution guards. 6d-b adds explicit state retention on tenure failure and holder migration from fuel boundaries. 6e extends backend layouts and transfer laws. Earlier static-safepoint-only lift prescriptions are historical. No compatibility promise is added.\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:12:`test/yin/vm/ucf/safepoint_harness_test.cljc`). Revision 2 (2026-10-11)\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:97:the safepoint harness · §6 code and task context in the carrier · §7\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:142:9. **Preemptive migration at any pc is a primary invariant of `yin.vm`** (owner, 2026-10-17: \\\\\\\"preemptive migration, the ability to pause and continue at any PC, is a primary invariant of yin.vm. It is why yin.vm is defined as a continuation VM based on the CESK model. The UCF being only defined at a wait or parked state is a violation of this invariant\\\\\\\"). The carrier expresses the evaluator's complete task state between **any** two instructions, including the scheduler's products (remaining waits, completed wakes), not only its two delivery states; a safepoint is a boundary at which the program stops by itself. Slices 6d-a (carrier, reference lane), 6d-b (holder, custody, expiry) and 6e (backends) land it.\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:640:frame from its state at a safepoint; `lift(lower(frame)) = frame` on\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1103:`:yin.k/not-at-safepoint` (UCF §7.4.2, as amended; the name is\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1110:`:yin.k/not-at-safepoint` rather than borrow its successor's pc.\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1202:## 5. The safepoint harness\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1208:module contexts and every refusal: lift at the safepoint, lower into a\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1210:uninterrupted reference run; `lift(lower(frame)) = frame`; the frame's\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1218:(`safepoint_harness_test.cljc:92-106`), whose expected results follow\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1230:the harness pins `1` for that one case (`safepoint_harness_test.cljc`,\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1268:of the old harness (`safepoint_harness_test.cljc:92-106`: `:bare`,\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1313:defined and otherwise refuses it `:export-missing`. **Amended 2026-10-16 (any-pc, owner invariant 2026-10-17).** A budgeted sweep can retain a child with active control at phase `:running`. Row 11 now obtains that state by real execution. The lower requires a `:running` child at phase `:running` and a `:blocked` child at phase `:parked`. Row 12 is row 10's child under tail delivery. No row promises an executable kind-`:parked` install child on\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1326:`:591-603`); `:yin.k/not-at-safepoint` (a register kernel stepped one\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1362:through `dvm/create-vm`/`rvm/create-vm`, run to the safepoint and lift\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1411:4. **Cross-engine canonical equality**: one program at one safepoint\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1515:6. `E` reconstruction: at every safepoint reached, the layout's `E`\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1528:9. Slices: for every non-tail safepoint with `m` return frames, the\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1725:`:yin.k/not-at-safepoint` when the kernel has an active continuation;\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1738:`image-segment` (§4.1), `:not-at-safepoint` of `safepoint!`,\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1742:`:ambiguous-image`, `:free-env-value` and `:not-at-safepoint` assert\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1864:(i) `rows/decode` of the wire under the budget (steps 1-7 of the\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2023:3. **Expiry and recovery.** Progress since the last durable checkpoint is lost on expiry; fuel makes the computation interruptible, exporting before the bound is what preserves it. Recovery lowers the checkpoint this holder received, or a durably authorized successor. Retained local progress receives no adoption, execution or publication authority. The source remains ended; `exit-mint` and abort cannot revive its tenure.\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2035:2. Exactly one raw budgeted action:\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2037:   - Otherwise, one budgeted scheduler round.\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2045:**Budgeted scheduler round.**\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2047:Propagate the budget through `check-wait-set`, `poll-links`, `advance-installs` and `advance-install`. Each visited child is invoked once through `run-fuel child n`; nested children use the same rule. Preserve existing gate stamping and the prohibition on running children under closed gates.\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2051:The dispatch tests **control presence**, not merely `engine/active-continuation?`: the latter only tests blocked/halted flags and can classify a control-less ingress-ready machine as active. Therefore no `run-fuel` path falls through `vm-hot` into its unbudgeted scheduler fallback. A quiescent control-less machine takes the budgeted no-work round and returns.\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2055:Each task visited during the invocation receives at most one budgeted action and at most one bridge step. Each task executes at most `n` guest instructions. For `t` distinct tasks visited during the invocation, including children created during the round, the instruction bound is `n × t`. No task is revisited with a fresh budget inside that invocation.\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2196:    [:cursor-cells]` under the default budget and 2 cells under\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2199:    `{:depth 3}` and under the default budget, and a literal nested 3000\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2205:    default budget; `{:work 1}` refuses `[:work]` at `emit` and, for a\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2207:22. Budgets: `:label-bytes` and `:search` gone, `:work` default\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2214:`test/yin/vm/semantic/safepoint_harness_test.cljc` (§5, the\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2351:    still refuses `:yin.k/not-at-safepoint`, and the same pc lifts as a\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2369:    `:not-at-safepoint` refusal belongs to a pc outside every body, not\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2478:10. **Budgeted children.** Preempt long and nested initializers; lift/lower running children under receiver admission; continue to linked. Count actual instruction transitions and assert at most `n` per visited task and `n × t` overall. No child receives a second budget inside one invocation.\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2480:11. **Bounded bridge execution.** A program repeatedly making bridge-served FFI calls returns from every `run-fuel` invocation. Each invocation executes at most one raw action and one bridge step. Repeated invocations reach the reference result. Diagnostic-only bridge input also returns after one step. Pin control-less ingress-ready dispatch to the budgeted round. For a pure active computation lasting at least `n` instructions, compare with `n` single-instruction steps; an earlier park/halt ends the comparison there.\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2498:diagnostics); `safepoint!`'s run mode (any pc inside a body);\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2515:refusing `:yin.k/not-at-safepoint`; item 6 resolved by the static check\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2546:  equals the saved set at non-tail safepoints (§5.6 item 5); the non-push\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2697:`[sp :yin.safepoint/stack-effect -1]` with `[sp :yin.safepoint/def #{…}]\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2698:[sp :yin.safepoint/use #{…}] [sp :yin.safepoint/live #{…}]`; in the\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2703:segment to each safepoint and compares the observed deltas and E-reads.\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2709:that runs the segment to each safepoint and compares the saved window's\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2726:**U6 — §7.11 (ACCEPT WITH CHANGES).** In \\\\\\\"Safepoint conformance\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2731:**cross-engine canonical equality**: one pr