cljc:533:(deftest ^:slow generator-depth-test\\\\ntest/yang/python/antlr/safepoint_test.cljc:554:(deftest ^:slow generator-admission-test\\\\ntest/yang/python/antlr/safepoint_test.cljc:593:(deftest ^:slow admission-in-every-mode-test\\\\ntest/yang/python/antlr/safepoint_test.cljc:616:(deftest ^:slow delegation-admission-test\\\\ntest/yang/python/antlr/safepoint_test.cljc:634:(deftest ^:slow generator-rebase-test\\\\ntest/yang/python/antlr/safepoint_test.cljc:650:(deftest ^:slow generator-throw-close-depth-test\\\\ntest/yang/python/antlr/safepoint_test.cljc:750:(deftest ^:slow set-recursion-limit-test\\\\ntest/yang/python/antlr/safepoint_test.cljc:817:(deftest ^:slow trace-basic-test\\\\ntest/yang/python/antlr/safepoint_test.cljc:832:(deftest ^:slow trace-basic-newlines-test\\\\nResults truncated to 100 lines (total: 306). Use offset=100 to see more.\\\"}\\ncollab/orch-lane/1793545000000-architect-p4-stress-budget-ruling.kimi-k3.1-pro.stdout.log:11:{\\\"role\\\":\\\"assistant\\\",\\\"tool_calls\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"function\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"tool_uRBKZXhRcjPPiKOkVgAaepiu\\\",\\\"function\\\":{\\\"name\\\":\\\"Grep\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":\\\"{\\\\\\\"pattern\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"safepoint|budget|Interrupt\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"path\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-php-p4/docs/design/yang.php.md\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"output_mode\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"content\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"-i\\\\\\\":true,\\\\\\\"-C\\\\\\\":5,\\\\\\\"head_limit\\\\\\\":200}\\\"}},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"function\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"tool_Edilczhzqd0VYboH5pd9NZbD\\\",\\\"function\\\":{\\\"name\\\":\\\"Read\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":\\\"{\\\\\\\"path\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-php-p4/docs/design/yin.vm.engine.md\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"line_offset\\\\\\\":535,\\\\\\\"n_lines\\\\\\\":55}\\\"}},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"function\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"tool_PNarCkmZm1e9npFlemCD6Qm6\\\",\\\"function\\\":{\\\"name\\\":\\\"Read\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":\\\"{\\\\\\\"path\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-php-p4/docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"line_offset\\\\\\\":650,\\\\\\\"n_lines\\\\\\\":48}\\\"}},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"function\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"tool_81bNtMQkr5Z0Thv7U8Ypjzob\\\",\\\"function\\\":{\\\"name\\\":\\\"Grep\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":\\\"{\\\\\\\"pattern\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"phpt-selection-runs-test|e2e-test|gc_013|gc_023\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"path\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-php-p4/test/yang/php\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"output_mode\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"content\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"-C\\\\\\\":5,\\\\\\\"head_limit\\\\\\\":150}\\\"}}]}\\ncollab/orch-lane/1793545000000-architect-p4-stress-budget-ruling.kimi-k3.1-pro.stdout.log:12:{\\\"role\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool_call_id\\\":\\\"tool_Edilczhzqd0VYboH5pd9NZbD\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"535\\\\texplicit roots connecting them. Reclaim only unreachable implementation\\\\n536\\\\tstorage, not stream history or persistent datoms. Avoid handle reuse\\\\n537\\\\tinitially; later reuse needs generations checked at every internal handle lookup.\\\\n538\\\\t\\\\n539\\\\tExternal state inspection produces immutable named-field snapshots. Resuming one\\\\n540\\\\tsnapshot cannot mutate another snapshot's frames, values, or state fields.\\\\n541\\\\tPersistent snapshots share immutable arena objects, never a mutable guest\\\\n542\\\\texecution buffer. The first implementation may copy the active state shadow\\\\n543\\\\tat every public IVM transition; optimize only after snapshot-alias tests pass.\\\\n544\\\\t\\\\n545\\\\t### E.3 Wasm stream implementation reference\\\\n546\\\\t\\\\n547\\\\tThe adapter surface, import signatures, outcome encoding, canonical Jing bytes\\\\n548\\\\tand buffer discipline live in [dao.stream.wasm.md](./dao.stream.wasm.md) §§1–3.\\\\n549\\\\tOwner decomposition, 2026-10-19: the former §E.3 content moved there unchanged;\\\\n550\\\\t§E.4 and §E.5 retain their numbers. Boundary doctrine and supersessions live in\\\\n551\\\\t[datom.world.abi.md](./datom.world.abi.md).\\\\n552\\\\t\\\\n553\\\\t### E.4 Composition adapters and the single in-instance engine\\\\n554\\\\t\\\\n555\\\\t#### E.4.1 Execution and embedding responsibilities\\\\n556\\\\t\\\\n557\\\\tNode/browser, Wasmtime and Wasmer provide the same stream implementation ([dao.stream.wasm.md](./dao.stream.wasm.md)).\\\\n558\\\\tThe composition hosts the imported adapters, their underlying stream\\\\n559\\\\timplementations and bridge interpreters;\\\\n560\\\\tit does not implement resolve-var, primitives, stores, GC, continuations or the\\\\n561\\\\tscheduler for wasm. A WASI-based composition may supply stream implementations through these\\\\n562\\\\tadapters; the VM core imports no WASI. There is no JS dependency in native runs.\\\\n563\\\\tThe CLJS engine is the reference oracle, not a second production wasm engine.\\\\n564\\\\t\\\\n565\\\\tThe in-instance engine owns run-loop/scheduler-round, step budgets, ready/wait\\\\n566\\\\tqueues and terminal checks. A step performs exactly one guest instruction; run\\\\n567\\\\tkeeps the original ready-queue/terminal ordering and returns on the same blocked,\\\\n568\\\\tparked or halted states. Blocking is a normal result. Inspection/test snapshots\\\\n569\\\\tare immutable data, not an external engine service contract. Runtime start/drive\\\\n570\\\\texports may only enter the in-instance driver; they are lifecycle controls, not\\\\n571\\\\tapplication callbacks. No wasm stack survives a wait.\\\\n572\\\\t\\\\n573\\\\t#### E.4.2 Single-engine-port rule and Rust reconciliation\\\\n574\\\\t\\\\n575\\\\tThe production engine **is** the Rust design's `yin-value`, `yin-scalar`,\\\\n576\\\\t`yin-image`, `yin-kernel`, `yin-prims`, `yin-engine`, `yin-wire` workspace\\\\n577\\\\t(`yin.vm.rust.md` §9), compiled to\\\\n578\\\\t`wasm32-unknown-unknown` and linked with compiled register bodies. The internal\\\\n579\\\\thandle facade adapts values, never reimplements semantics. Native wrappers\\\\n580\\\\timplement only stream adapters and runtime mechanics. No parallel engine port\\\\n581\\\\tis permitted to bypass a crate's missing wasm support.\\\\n582\\\\t\\\\n583\\\\t“One transition implementation, two dispatchers” applies to the Rust interpreter,\\\\n584\\\\tcompiled wasm bodies and future LLVM helpers (`yin.vm.rust.md` §7.4 and §12 risk 2).\\\\n585\\\\tGenerated control flow uses shared transition helpers for call/return/restore/\\\\n586\\\\teffects; no wrapper duplicates them. CLJS necessarily has a language-port\\\\n587\\\\timplementation: it remains the shared-kit oracle, not literally the same binary.\\\\n588\\\\tCheck-then-commit, refused-step equality and per-machine fault containment remain\\\\n589\\\\tmandatory (`yin.vm.rust.md` §§5.3–5.5). Panics are kernel defects,\\\"}\\ncollab/orch-lane/1793545000000-architect-p4-stress-budget-ruling.kimi-k3.1-pro.stdout.log:14:{\\\"role\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool_call_id\\\":\\\"tool_uRBKZXhRcjPPiKOkVgAaepiu\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"docs/design/yang.php.md-91-to D7, the shared rulings (own null sentinel, Jing numeric kinds, JVM-only\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-92-parsing with three-host execution, the linked-profile matrix of bundled on\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-93-four evaluators and linked on three until L-b), and the ADR 0004 dependency.\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-94-PHP uses the lifted namespaces of `yang.typescript.md` section 17 (L1 to L4\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-95-land first) and adds nothing to them (section 16). Two PHP-specific\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:96:dependencies: statement-level ticks wait on safepoint slice 3 (section 12),\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-97-and optional absent includes wait on the known-gaps ledger item for\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-98-publication-time-unavailable imports (section 11.3).\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-99-\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-100-## 3. The paradigm specification\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-101-\\\\n--\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1234-|    |                                    | order, then the static tables,     |\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1235-|    |                                    | then `FREE` every remaining object |\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1236-|    |                                    | without calling destructors. An    |\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1237-|    |                                    | uncaught `Throwable` runs this     |\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1238-|    |                                    | sequence after the error output;   |\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:1239:|    |                                    | the VM's operational halts (budget |\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1240-|    |                                    | exhaustion, cancellation) skip the |\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1241-|    |                                    | destructor phase, as Zend skips it |\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1242-|    |                                    | on fatal errors                    |\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1243-+----+------------------------------------+------------------------------------+\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1244-\\\\n--\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1395-Z-combinator per function and per loop, type hints parsed and dropped, `-10;`\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1396-folded into a literal, and PHP `null` lowered to host `nil`. Its tokenizer has\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1397-no modes (no HTML, no heredoc, no `<?=`). Replacing only its parser would keep\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1398-every semantic defect. **Ruling: replace.** Nothing of the legacy lowering is\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1399-reused; the Z-combinator encoding is superseded by self-applied `:loop`-marked\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:1400:lambdas with cells, which also makes safepoints and tail marks work.\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1401-\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1402-Migration mechanics (the F2 pattern):\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1403-\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1404-- The ANTLR frontend is installed in `yin.repl.frontends/standard` as a\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1405-  new revision of `:yang/php` (the compiler frontend keeps its revision\\\\n--\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1916-   throw `Error` with PHP's fatal text. The warning text retains the written\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1917-   kind. A refused path is not added to the included-files dict, so a later\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1918-   `_once` retries delivery. Each record carries the structured refusal under\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1919-   `:yang.php/refusal`.\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1920-\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:1921:## 12. Safepoints\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1922-\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1923-- `:loop` and `:call` hooks (`phpsp`) serve signals: `pcntl_signal` handlers\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1924-  run at hooks via `stream/poll!` on a signal stream, and\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1925-  `pcntl_async_signals` is the default and only mode. A recursion-depth bound\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1926-  is available if a composition wants one (PHP has none; default off).\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1927-- `max_execution_time` and `set_time_limit` are wall-clock in PHP and so\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:1928:  nondeterministic: the profile offers a deterministic **safepoint-count\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:1929:  budget** instead, raising the fatal with PHP's text, a recorded departure\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1930-  (owner decision B8.5, corner C21).\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1931-- **Statement ticks** (`declare(ticks=N)`, `register_tick_function`) need\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:1932:  `:line` sites before non-lambda statement nodes. `yang.safepoint` currently\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1933-  refuses a selected site that is not a `:lambda` (`site-not-lambda`), and\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:1934:  `:line` insertion is safepoint slice 3, which Python tracing also needs.\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1935-  Ticks therefore **depend on the shared `:line` extension**: P7 splits into\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:1936:  P7-a (signals, no dependency) and P7-b (ticks, behind safepoint slice 3).\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:1937:  Neither L1 to L4 nor this frontend extends `yang.safepoint`; the extension\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:1938:  is the safepoint seat's.\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1939-- No thread switches: PHP is single-threaded, and one request is one task.\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1940-\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1941-## 13. Diagnostics\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1942-\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1943-Compile time: `:yang.php/syntax`; `:yang.php/unsupported {:construct}`;\\\\n--\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1965-  by-reference, defaults, variadics, coercion versus `strict_types`); classes\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1966-  (trait precedence, visibility, late static binding, magic methods, readonly,\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1967-  enums, `match`, destructors, `clone`); exceptions (`finally` ordering,\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1968-  multi-catch, the `Error` hierarchy); generators; request (superglobals from\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1969-  a fixture record, headers after output, `ob_*`); inclusion (`_once`, return\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:1970:  values, scope sharing, the two missing-include stages); safepoints (tick\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1971-  counts, a signal at a hook).\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1972-- **Fixture groups** are those of section 4.6, plus a request-record fixture\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1973-  per corpus program. Corners are departure fixtures whose expected value is\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1974-  the recorded deviation.\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-1975-\\\\n--\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2090-|       |                                  | `require_once` throw `Error`; a   |\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2091-|       |                                  | refused `_once` retries delivery  |\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2092-+-------+----------------------------------+-----------------------------------+\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2093-| P7-a  | signals: `phpsp` hooks at        | a signal at a `:loop` hook runs   |\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2094-|       | `:loop` and `:call`,             | the handler; an empty signal      |\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:2095:|       | `pcntl_signal`, the safepoint    | stream never parks; budget        |\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:2096:|       | budget                           | exhaustion raises the pinned      |\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2097-|       |                                  | fatal text                        |\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2098-+-------+----------------------------------+-----------------------------------+\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2099-| P7-b  | ticks: `declare(ticks)`,         | tick counts equal PHP's for the   |\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2100-|       | `register_tick_function`; behind | statement fixture                 |\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:2101:|       | safepoint slice 3                |                                   |\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2102-+-------+----------------------------------+-----------------------------------+\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2103-| P8    | legacy retirement: the legacy    | the REPL prints `1` for `<?php $x |\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2104-|       | test programs in the new corpus, | = 1; echo $x;`; every legacy test |\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2105-|       | the demo on checked-in CST       | program passes with corrected     |\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2106-|       | packets,                         | expectations; the demo runs its   |\\\\n--\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2315-|                     | in P4                               |                  |\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2316-+---------------------+-------------------------------------+------------------+\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2317-| C21 memory and time | Engine: `memory_limit`,             | restricted; none |\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2318-| limits              | `max_execution_time`,               | (operational)    |\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2319-|                     | `memory_get_usage`. Here: the       |                  |\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:2320:|                     | deterministic safepoint budget and  |                  |\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2321-|                     | no memory accounting;               |                  |\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2322-|                     | `memory_get_usage` returns a pinned |                  |\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2323-|                     | constant                            |                  |\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2324-+---------------------+-------------------------------------+------------------+\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2325-| C22 destructor      | Engine: destructor `echo` inside an | specified,       |\\\\n--\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2472-3. (B8.3) The dynamic-scope profile rule (recommended) versus dict scopes for\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2473-   every function (simpler, slower, and it loses the cell path).\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2474-4. (B8.4) Warnings as diagnostic-stream records (recommended) versus a guest\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2475-   `Warning` exception class; the record model matches ADR 0004 and keeps `@`\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2476-   cheap.\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:2477:5. (B8.5) The deterministic safepoint budget as the `max_execution_time`\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2478-   stand-in (recommended) versus refusing the ini.\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2479-6. (B8.6) Replace and delete the compiler frontend at P8 (recommended) versus\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2480-   keeping the compiler revision of `:yang/php` installed until a later date.\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2481-7. (B8.7) The autoload class-map rule (recommended) versus refusing\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2482-   `spl_autoload_register` in Phase 3.\\\\n--\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-2518-|                             | grammar (generics refused); semantics: the     |\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-25