r-str (:profile requirement))\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc:271:                \\\\\\\" is noninterruptible: imported without a site set\\\\\\\")}\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc-272-\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc-273-    (:hooks requirement)\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc-274-    (if (empty? record-addresses)\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc-275-      (refusal :yang.python.antlr/missing-site-set requirement\\\\n--\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc-298-                     (assoc defect :manifest manifest :record a))))))\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc-299-\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc-300-    :else\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc-301-    (refusal :yang.python.antlr/profile-undeclared requirement\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc:302:             \\\\\\\"the profile declares neither :hooks nor :noninterruptible\\\\\\\"\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc-303-             {:manifest manifest})))\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc-304-\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc-305-\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc-306-;; =============================================================================\\\\n--\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc-501-\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc-502-(defn stage\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc-503-  \\\\\\\"The link-time stage (`yin.vm.linker.interpreter/composition`'s `:stage`)\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc-504-   of a Python import under `requirement`: `{:profile name :hooks true\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc:505:   :hooks-profile p :pysp address}` or `{:profile name :noninterruptible\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc-506-   true}`, with `:runtime` the names of the runtime modules (default `py`,\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc-507-   `pysp`) it passes through. `records` ({manifest [record-address ...]})\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc-508-   are the local publication's records; a DHT source supplies none and the\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc-509-   stage discovers them from the index datoms of its context. The stage\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc-510-   reads only the context's `:store` and never fetches: it answers\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc-511-   `{:status :missing :address a}` for the first address that store does\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc-512-   not hold, and is run again once it is there. Answers\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc-513-   `(fn [ctx name address])`: `{:status :ok :address address}` as published\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc:514:   when noninterruptible, else the address of the instrumented module\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc-515-   derived bottom-up from the verified sets (`:derivation` its `:derive`\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc-516-   record's address), or the refusal naming the profile, the set and the\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc-517-   `:name` refused.\\\\\\\"\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc-518-  [registry requirement records]\\\\n--\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc-520-    (fn [ctx name address]\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc-521-      (cond\\\\nResults truncated to 150 lines (total: 301). Use offset=150 to see more.\\\"}\\ncollab/orch-lane/1793545000000-architect-p4-stress-budget-ruling.kimi-k3.1-pro.stdout.log:22:{\\\"role\\\":\\\"assistant\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"## Ruling: both, sequenced\\\\n\\\\n**(b) Re-tier immediately.** Keep ordinary PHPT cases in the quick tier, but move the curated PHPT stress cases—at minimum `gc_013`, `gc_023`, and their e2e-derived counterparts—behind `^:slow` / `DATOM_SLOW_TESTS`. Do not reduce iteration counts or otherwise alter fixture semantics. The current combined quick test is at `test/yang/php/antlr/e2e_test.clj:340`.\\\\n\\\\n**(a) Add the budget as a separate P7-a robustness change, not as a prerequisite for lane stability.**\\\\n\\\\nSmallest contract:\\\\n\\\\n- Add an **optional, per-run safepoint-count budget** to the PHP execution profile. `run-vm` may pass the option, but must not implement a host wall-clock timeout as guest semantics.\\\\n- Count the existing PHP `:loop` and `:call` safepoint hooks; do not introduce generic VM-instruction accounting for this feature.\\\\n- Default is **unlimited/off**, so production behavior is unchanged unless a composition explicitly supplies a budget.\\\\n- Exhaustion is the documented **PHP operational fatal**, using the pinned PHP text—not the JavaScript `Interrupt` exception. It is not guest-catchable and skips destructor shutdown, consistent with `docs/design/yang.php.md:1239` and `docs/design/yang.php.md:1927`.\\\\n- This bounds guest execution between hooks; it is not a wall-clock guarantee around blocking host operations.\\\\n\\\\nThis follows the existing PHP contract: deterministic safepoint budget rather than nondeterministic `max_execution_time` (`docs/design/yang.php.md:1921-1938`, `docs/design/yang.php.md:2093-2097`). Generic engine step budgets remain an engine responsibility (`docs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:565-568`); safepoints are program stopping boundaries, not a license to change default execution semantics (`docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:655-659`).\\\\n\\\\n**Disposition of the 93-minute shiva sighting:** close the suspected **guest-nontermination defect now** as finite stress cost, supported by the fixture walk and measured `gc_013` completion (`collab/1793540000000-engineer-p4-hang.gpt-6-luna.findings.md:9-21`). Keep the **quick-tier lane-stability task** open until re-tiering lands; do not hold the hang investigation open for the budget work.\\\"}\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_23\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba 