{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import json; p=\\\"collab/orch-lane/1794680000000-architect-consolidated-round.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log\\\"; ds=(json.loads(l) for l in open(p) if l.startswith(\\\"{\\\")); print(\\\"\\\\n\\\".join(d.get(\\\"item\\\",{}).get(\\\"text\\\", \\\"\\\") for d in ds if d.get(\\\"item\\\",{}).get(\\\"type\\\")==\\\"agent_message\\\"))'\"","aggregated_output":"python3: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\npython3: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-5JLNBc52' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n2026-11-05 13:42:27.299 xcodebuild[33310:110547554]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-11-05 13:42:27.654 xcodebuild[33310:110547553] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\npython3: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\npython3: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-7xS9R3bP' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n2026-11-05 13:42:28.546 xcodebuild[33314:110547573]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-11-05 13:42:28.871 xcodebuild[33314:110547572] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\nI’ll read the architecture rules and the four worktree diffs, then issue the three verdicts with file-and-line evidence and landing authority. I’ll keep this pass read-only and leave behavioral validation to the recorded shiva gates.\n\nI’m applying the repository’s `code-review-pr` skill, using your requested verdict format and static-only scope.\n\nTwo concrete issues have surfaced: the P5 fold commit has malformed fixture calls that the laptop working tree repairs, and the P1 shutdown fallback references `fesc` outside its lexical binding. I’m tracing whether that shutdown branch is reachable and checking the terminal escape and include boundaries before deciding landing authority.\n\nThe terminal escape bypasses guest handlers and finalizers as intended. The out-of-scope `fesc` also creates a free name in the linked PHP module, so the bundled safepoint tests do not establish that includes still work. The P5 diagnostics need separate rulings: missing diagnostics are engine behavior; location text and errno classification are different comparison concerns.\n\nP8’s quick manifest is internally consistent: 95 unique mismatch IDs, matching descriptions and family counts, plus eight slow-gap records. But three slow records still expect undefined `str_repeat` or `str_replace` after the merged P9 tree registers both builtins. Those records need fresh measurements on the merged tree. The cell-reference change looks sound, including the shared callable fallback.\n\nThe landing decision is now clear: the cell-reference branch can land; P1, P8, and P5 need forward fixes. One additional P1 edge remains: `exit()` inside a shutdown callback escapes past the new buffer drain, so an open buffer can still lose output. I’m consolidating the exact fixes and the three diagnostic rulings.\n\n**Verdict 1 — DEFECT: `0eade311` needs another forward fix.**\n\n- **Exhaustion escape: CONFIRMED.** `php/abandon-to` only pops frames; it executes no guest finalizers. The captured continuation then bypasses guest handlers and returns. [prelude.cljc:214](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p1fix/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:214)\n- **Shutdown termination: CONFIRMED-WITH-EDITS.** Safepoint exhaustion reaches the stored fatal continuation during shutdown. However, the operational-`exc2` fallback calls **out-of-scope `fesc`**. Replace that call with `(php/root-fatal (get exc2 :message))`. [prelude.cljc:5189](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p1fix/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:5189)\n- **Budget domain: CONFIRMED.** The constructor rejects negative integers, fractional values, strings, and other nonintegers with named host-side `:invalid-budget`. Zero is admitted. [safepoint.cljc:43](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p1fix/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/safepoint.cljc:43)\n\n**The include-unit boundary regresses even with unlimited execution.** The stray `fesc` becomes a free name in the PHP runtime module; module publication rejects undeclared names before execution. This is independent of whether the fallback executes. [prelude.cljc:5505](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p1fix/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:5505), [core/prelude.cljc:152](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p1fix/src/cljc/yang/core/prelude.cljc:152). The bundled harness still leaves the AST uninstrumented when no budget is supplied. [e2e_harness.clj:97](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p1fix/test/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj:97)\n\nThe additional Round-A repairs are partly confirmed: ordinary `exit` now skips guest `finally` and preserves status; normal shutdown drains nested buffers. **Buffer draining remains defective when a shutdown callback exits.** For example, `ob_start(); register_shutdown_function(function(){ echo 'S'; exit(3); }); echo 'A';` escapes past the drain and renders buffer zero, losing buffered output. Move mandatory buffer draining outside the shutdown escape, while retaining the operational-fatal bypass. [prelude.cljc:485](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p1fix/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:485), [prelude.cljc:3942](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p1fix/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:3942), [prelude.cljc:5195](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p1fix/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:5195)\n\n**Verdict 2 — CONFIRMED-WITH-EDITS: the three design rulings.**\n\n- **(a) Empty `ob_end_clean`: engine implementation gap.** Preserve the recorded notice. Change the no-buffer arm to emit `php/warn` with errno **8** and the recorded message, then return `false`. Do not normalize away a missing diagnostic: handlers and reporting masks can observe it. [prelude.cljc:390](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p5r/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:390)\n- **(b) Headers-already-sent text: permit narrow comparison normalization.** Strip only the location suffix ` by (output started at …:line)` from the oracle message. Preserve the warning, errno, and message prefix; retain the full raw observation. The engine’s deliberate shorter form may remain. [prelude.cljc:404](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p5r/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:404), [programs_p5.cljc:52](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p5r/test/yang/php/antlr/programs_p5.cljc:52)\n- **(c) 1024 versus 8: runner classification artifact; engine stays 1024.** `\"Notice\"→8` cannot identify `E_USER_NOTICE`. Preserve the old observation as explicitly class-derived; keep the engine semantic expectation at **1024**. Until exact errno recording replaces it, permit **1024→8 only in comparison against marked class-derived observations**, not as a global diagnostic rewrite. [oracle.clj:36](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p5r/src/dev/yang/php/oracle.clj:36), [oracle.clj:98](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p5r/src/dev/yang/php/oracle.clj:98)\n\n**Verdict 3(a) — DEFECT: P8 at `bab43c51`.**\n\nThe legacy compiler deletion and executable-reference sweep are complete. The REPL and demo use the ANTLR route, and subsystem routing is retargeted. The migrated corpus uses PHP expectations with an honest hand-derived banner. [frontends.cljc:83](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p8/src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc:83), [subsystems.edn:62](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p8/src/dev/subsystems.edn:62), [programs_p8.cljc:6](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p8/test/yang/php/antlr/programs_p8.cljc:6)\n\nThe quick manifest is internally consistent: **95 unique IDs**, matching description keys; families **10 GC / 16 foreach-by-reference / 3 unset / 3 named / 63 other**; recorded unsupported count **57**. All eight slow records match their selection entries’ expectation fields. [manifest.edn:90](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p8/test/yang/php/antlr/phpt_quick_mismatch_manifest.edn:90)\n\n**Blocking defect:** slow records `bug44069`, `bug40809`, and `bug63055` still expect undefined `str_repeat`/`str_replace`, although the merged tree registers and implements both. Remeasure those three on the merged tree; remove records that now pass or record their actual remaining failure. Do not infer replacement outcomes from static reading. [manifest.edn:45](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p8/test/yang/php/antlr/phpt_quick_mismatch_manifest.edn:45), [manifest.edn:79](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p8/test/yang/php/antlr/phpt_quick_mismatch_manifest.edn:79), [builtins.cljc:56](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p8/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/builtins.cljc:56)\n\n**Verdict 3(b) — DEFECT: P5 fold at `3a2ce4da`.**\n\nRequired edits:\n\n- **Commit the existing laptop fixture repair.** The committed fold puts metadata before the positional output argument and closes calls prematurely; the working-tree diff repairs those malformed forms. The repaired file is still uncommitted. [programs_p5.cljc:37](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p5r/test/yang/php/antlr/programs_p5.cljc:37)\n- Apply Verdict 2 consistently to oracle and engine comparisons. The current engine gate compares diagnostics literally, so the repaired fixtures still disagree on the three ruled cases. [request_context_test.clj:23](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p5r/test/yang/php/antlr/request_context_test.clj:23)\n- Fix `request-pairs` to accept ordered entry vectors. The engine accepts them; the runner silently turns them into empty arrays. For the current typed-array fixture, insertion order, server-field replacement, and GET-then-POST merge construction agree. [oracle.clj:227](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p5r/src/dev/yang/php/oracle.clj:227), [prelude.cljc:335](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p5r/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:335)\n- Compare fixture `:status` against process `:exit`; currently the runner discards it, leaving the exit-status pins unverified. [oracle.clj:292](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p5r/src/dev/yang/php/oracle.clj:292)\n- Attach P5 run provenance. The fold printer inherits P3-b’s banner rather than establishing the P5 run’s version/host/date. [oracle.clj:31](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p5r/src/dev/yang/php/oracle.clj:31), [oracle.clj:324](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p5r/src/dev/yang/php/oracle.clj:324)\n\n**Verdict 3(c) — CONFIRMED: cellref sweep at `1636e3e9`.**\n\nAuthentication precedes shape-based dereferencing. Inauthentic shapes reach ordinary descriptor handling, whose shared implementation also authenticates before dereferencing. Genuine object/function/symbol routing is preserved. The regression pairs cover `typeof`/`kind-of` and receiver propagation with shaped data versus genuine references. [prelude.cljc:135](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cs/src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude.cljc:135), [call.cljc:28](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cs/src/cljc/yang/core/call.cljc:28), [prelude_test.cljc:689](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cs/test/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude_test.cljc:689)\n\n**Landing authority:** `feat/cellref-sweep` may merge now. Hold `feat/p1-forward-fixes`, `feat/p8-legacy-retirement`, and `feat/p5-oracle-recording` for the fixes above and the seat’s corresponding gates. Static review only; no behavioral suites run and no files changed.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
