{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat AGENTS.md; ls .cpcache; sed -n '1,95p' test/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj; sed -n '1,55p' test/yang/php/antlr/portable_harness.cljc; sed -n '1,90p' deps.edn\"","aggregated_output":"# ==============================================================================\n# datom.world – Development Rules & Architectural Foundations\n# ==============================================================================\n\nSee [`docs/design/datom.world.md`](./docs/design/datom.world.md) for master architecture, core philosophy, foundational axioms, non-negotiable invariants, code style, development workflow, and operational guides (testing, team roles, agent delegation, website formats).\n2072761871.basis\n2072761871.cp\n2072761871.main\n2276128749.basis\n2276128749.cp\n4183786633.basis\n4183786633.cp\n4183786633.jvm\n4183786633.main\n4183786633.manifest\n868029096.basis\n868029096.cp\n868029096.main\n(ns yang.php.antlr.e2e-harness\n  \"The JVM end-to-end harness: PHP source -> CST packet -> lowering stage ->\n   program envelope -> the bundled program on each of the four VMs. Output\n   is the unit's bottom buffer, a latin-1 byte carrier, decoded as UTF-8\n   here at the boundary.\"\n  (:require\n    [clojure.walk :as walk]\n    [dao.host.text :as text]\n    [dao.stream :as stream]\n    [yang.php.antlr.cst :as cst]\n    [yang.php.antlr.lower :as lower]\n    [yang.php.antlr.portable-harness :as portable]\n    [yang.php.antlr.safepoint :as hooks]\n    [yang.core.uast :as u]\n    [yang.safepoint :as safepoint]\n    [yin.vm :as vm]\n    [yin.vm.debruijn.register :as rvm]\n    [yin.vm.debruijn.stack :as dvm]\n    [yin.vm.encoder :as encoder]\n    [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]\n    [yin.vm.semantic.derive :as derive]\n    [yin.vm.semantic.linearize :as sr-linearize]\n    [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]))\n\n\n(defn host-registry\n  \"The registry the PHP compositions run over.\"\n  []\n  (portable/host-registry))\n\n\n(def ^:private base-opts\n  {:make-stream tu/make-stream,\n   :capability-secret tu/secret,\n   :primitives vm/primitives})\n\n\n(def ^:private load-semantic\n  (vm/fresh-code-loader semantic/load-ast vm/ast-contract))\n\n\n(defn lower-program\n  \"`{:ast a :warnings w}` for `source` through the lowering stage, or\n   `{:diagnostics d}`. Warning-severity diagnostics do not stop the program.\"\n  [source]\n  (let [cst-log (tu/new-memory-log)\n        program (tu/new-memory-log)\n        diagnostics (tu/new-memory-log)]\n    (stream/append! cst-log (cst/parse-source source))\n    (lower/step-stage (lower/open-stage cst-log program diagnostics\n                                        {:medium lower/program-medium}))\n    (let [{warnings true, problems false}\n          (group-by #(= :warning (:severity %)) (tu/drain diagnostics))]\n      (if (seq problems)\n        {:diagnostics problems}\n        (let [{:yin/keys [batch root] :as envelope} (first (tu/drain program))]\n          {:ast (nth batch root), :envelope envelope, :warnings (vec warnings)})))))\n\n\n(defn packet->form\n  \"The nested form of a CST packet, spans dropped: `[:rule child ...]` for a\n   rule, `[\\\"TYPE\\\" \\\"text\\\"]` for a token. The inverse of\n   `portable-harness/packet`.\"\n  [{:yang.cst/keys [root nodes]}]\n  (letfn [(form\n            [id]\n            (let [{:keys [kind rule type text children]} (nth nodes id)]\n              (if (= :token kind)\n                [type text]\n                (into [(keyword rule)] (map form) children))))]\n    (form root)))\n\n\n(defn latin1->text\n  \"The UTF-8 text of the byte carrier `s`.\"\n  [s]\n  (text/utf8-decode (.getBytes ^String s \"ISO-8859-1\")))\n\n\n(defn render\n  \"The text a unit prints: its output, then, for an uncaught error, the\n   fatal line (no path, plan section 3.9).\"\n  [{:php/keys [out uncaught fatal]}]\n  (str (latin1->text out)\n       (when uncaught\n         (str \"PHP Fatal error:  Uncaught \" (:class uncaught) \": \" (:message uncaught)))\n       (when fatal\n         (str \"PHP Fatal error:  \" fatal))))\n\n\n(defn run-vms\n  \"`{vm-key rendered}` of `ast` on the four VMs; a host throw is\n   `[:thrown message]`. `:execution-budget` derives the PHP safepoint hooks\n   and starts one per-run counter; no option leaves the AST unchanged.\"\n  ([registry ast] (run-vms registry ast {}))\n(ns yang.php.antlr.portable-harness\n  \"What the JVM, Node and Dart lanes share: the host composition the PHP\n   profile runs over, the `packet` helper that builds a CST packet from a\n   nested form, and a parserless run of a packet on the AST walker.\"\n  (:require\n    [dao.stream :as stream]\n    [dao.stream.memory-log :as memory-log]\n    [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ringbuffer]\n    [yang.php.antlr.lower :as lower]\n    [yang.php.antlr.prelude :as prelude]\n    [yin.vm :as vm]\n    [yin.vm.ast-walker :as ast-walker]\n    [yin.vm.data :as data]\n    [yin.vm.integer :as integer]\n    [yin.vm.module :as module]))\n\n\n(def ^:private capability-secret \"yin.vm.test-utils/capability-secret\")\n\n\n(defn create-vm\n  \"An AST walker composed with the harness's deterministic ring-buffer stream.\"\n  ([] (create-vm {}))\n  ([opts]\n   (ast-walker/create-vm\n     (merge {:make-stream\n             (fn [capacity]\n               (ringbuffer/create!\n                 {:dao.stream/type ringbuffer/transport-type,\n                  ringbuffer/capacity-key (or capacity vm/default-stream-capacity)}))\n             :capability-secret capability-secret}\n            opts))))\n\n\n(defn- new-memory-log\n  []\n  (let [result (memory-log/create! {:dao.stream/type memory-log/transport-type})]\n    (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome result))\n      (:dao.stream/handle result)\n      (throw (ex-info \"PHP harness memory-log creation failed\" {:result result})))))\n\n\n(defn- drain\n  [handle]\n  (let [start (get-in (stream/cursor handle stream/anchor-oldest)\n                      [:dao.stream/cursor])]\n    (loop [cursor start, acc []]\n      (let [result (stream/next handle cursor)]\n        (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome result))\n          (recur (:dao.stream/cursor result)\n                 (conj acc (:dao.stream/value result)))\n          acc)))))\n\n\n(def integer-limits\n{:deps {org.clojure/core.async {:mvn/version \"1.8.741\"}\n        org.clojure/tools.reader {:mvn/version \"1.5.0\"}\n        ring/ring {:mvn/version \"1.14.1\"}\n        com.cognitect/transit-clj {:mvn/version \"1.0.333\"}\n        org.replikativ/boring {:mvn/version \"0.1.30\"}\n        com.datomic/peer {:mvn/version \"1.0.7364\"}\n        org.postgresql/postgresql {:mvn/version \"42.7.3\"}\n        org.clojure/data.json {:mvn/version \"2.5.0\"}\n        http-kit/http-kit {:mvn/version \"2.8.0\"}\n        org.jsoup/jsoup {:mvn/version \"1.18.3\"}\n        instaparse/instaparse {:mvn/version \"1.5.0\"}\n        ;; yang.python.antlr: the runtime the generated Python3 parser runs\n        ;; on; pinned to the tool version in :antlr-gen (they are one release)\n        org.antlr/antlr4-runtime {:mvn/version \"4.13.2\"}\n        criterium/criterium {:mvn/version \"0.4.6\"}\n        io.github.rctcwyvrn/blake3 {:mvn/version \"1.3\"}\n        stigmergy/chp {:mvn/version \"0.1.0-SNAPSHOT\"\n                       :exclusions [refactor-nrepl/refactor-nrepl]}}\n :cljd/opts {}\n ;; build/antlr/python3/classes: the generated Python3 parser, produced by\n ;; `clj -M:antlr-gen` (antlr/python3/manifest.edn); absent until generated\n :paths [\"src/clj\" \"src/cljc\" \"src/cljs\" \"src/cljd\"\n         \"build/antlr/python3/classes\" \"build/antlr/php/classes\"\n         \"build/antlr/typescript/classes\"]\n :aliases {:clean {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                   :exec-fn clean/clean}\n           :profile-btree {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                           :extra-deps {persistent-sorted-set/persistent-sorted-set\n                                        {:mvn/version \"0.3.0\"}}\n                           :main-opts [\"-m\" \"btree-bench\"]}\n           :test {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n                  :extra-deps {io.github.cognitect-labs/test-runner\n                               {:git/tag \"v0.5.1\" :git/sha \"dfb30dd\"}\n                               ;; latte-kernel: the LaTTe proof assistant's kernel,\n                               ;; the differential oracle for the yang.clojure gap\n                               ;; program (pinned; MIT; dependency-free)\n                               latte-kernel/latte-kernel\n                               {:git/url \"https://github.com/latte-central/latte-kernel\"\n                                :git/sha \"86fca0d1d054af005cb37395eae04500d45e6279\"}}\n                  ;; The guest recursion limit allows depth that needs more than the\n                  ;; JVM's platform default thread stack (1024 KB on Linux, 2048 KB on\n                  ;; macOS): under 1 MB the guard loses to a JVM StackOverflowError\n                  ;; before it can raise Python's RecursionError, so the same tests\n                  ;; pass on macOS and fail on Linux. 4 MB is twice the measured\n                  ;; macOS-default minimum, leaving headroom as the prelude grows.\n                  ;; Evidence: docs/agents/known-gaps.md (the recursion rows).\n                  ;; merged stack policy: -Xss64m supersedes the earlier -Xss4m —\n                  ;; deep assertion payloads (the PHPT selection diagnostics and\n                  ;; the conformance compositions) overflow smaller stacks in\n                  ;; clojure.test's printer on shiva (verified green at -Xss64m;\n                  ;; the 4m minimum for the prelude recursion rows still holds)\n                  :jvm-opts [\"-Xss64m\"]\n                  :main-opts [\"-m\" \"cognitect.test-runner\"]\n                  :exec-fn cognitect.test-runner.api/test}\n           :nREPL {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n                   :extra-deps {nrepl/nrepl {:mvn/version \"1.0.0\"}\n                                cider/cider-nrepl {:mvn/version \"0.58.0\"}}\n                   :main-opts [\"-m\" \"nrepl.cmdline\" \"--middleware\" \"[cider.nrepl/cider-middleware]\"]}\n           :cljs {:extra-paths [\"test\" \"src/dev\" \"build/antlr/python3/js\"]\n                  :extra-deps {thheller/shadow-cljs {:mvn/version \"3.3.5\"}\n                               reagent/reagent {:mvn/version \"2.0.1\"}\n                               com.cognitect/transit-cljs {:mvn/version \"0.8.280\"}}}\n           :dev {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                 :extra-deps {thheller/shadow-cljs {:mvn/version \"3.3.5\"}\n                              cider/cider-nrepl {:mvn/version \"0.58.0\"}\n                              reagent/reagent {:mvn/version \"2.0.1\"}\n                              com.cognitect/transit-cljs {:mvn/version \"0.8.280\"}\n                              ;; benchmark baseline + psset-fixtures\n                              ;; generator only; production uses\n                              ;; dao.data.btree\n                              persistent-sorted-set/persistent-sorted-set\n                              {:mvn/version \"0.3.0\"}}\n                 :jvm-opts [\"-Dconfig=config.clj\"]}\n           ;; The one ClojureDart pin. Compose it with the build aliases:\n           ;; clj -M:clojuredart:cljd ..., clj -M:clojuredart:cljd-yin-repl-build ...\n           :clojuredart {:extra-deps {sonwh98/clojuredart\n                                      {:git/url \"https://github.com/sonwh98/ClojureDart.git\"\n                                       :sha \"7d00ee2aa7fa9d990581e78ebc4a66b93cb70a31\"}\n                                      }}\n           :cljd {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n                  :main-opts [\"-m\" \"cljd.build\"]\n                  :cljd/opts {:kind :flutter :main datomworld.demo.main}}\n           :server {:extra-deps {http-kit/http-kit {:mvn/version \"2.8.0\"}}\n                    :jvm-opts [\"-Dconfig=config.clj\"]\n                    :main-opts [\"-m\" \"world.server\"]}\n           :clj-yin-repl {:main-opts [\"-m\" \"yin.repl.main\"]}\n           ;; jolt host configuration (docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md\n           ;; §4.2-4.3), run through build/tools/jolt/bin/jolt -Srepro -M:jolt.\n           ;; src/jolt precedes src/cljc so a host override wins; src/clj is\n           ;; listed for audited portable namespaces only (its JVM namespaces\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_31","type":"web_search","id":"exec-73fe6791-6368-421b-a491-ca068caefba8","query":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/php/php-src/PHP-8.3/ext/json/json.c","action":{"type":"open_page","url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/php/php-src/PHP-8.3/ext/json/json.c"},"results":[{"type":"text_result","domain":"raw.githubusercontent.com","ref_id":"turn2view0","snippet":"Total lines: 349","url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/php/php-src/PHP-8.3/ext/json/json.c"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"raw.githubusercontent.com","ref_id":"turn2view1","snippet":"Total lines: 6486","url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/php/php-src/PHP-8.3/ext/standard/array.c"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"raw.githubusercontent.com","ref_id":"turn2view2","snippet":"Total lines: 6486","url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/php/php-src/PHP-8.3/ext/standard/array.c"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"raw.githubusercontent.com","ref_id":"turn2view3","snippet":"Total lines: 6486","url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/php/php-src/PHP-8.3/ext/standard/array.c"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"raw.githubusercontent.com","ref_id":"turn2view4","snippet":"Total lines: 384","url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/php/php-src/PHP-8.3/ext/json/json_scanner.re"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"raw.githubusercontent.com","ref_id":"turn2view5","snippet":"Total lines: 384","url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/php/php-src/PHP-8.3/ext/json/json_scanner.re"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"www.php.net","ref_id":"turn2view6","snippet":"Total lines: 1464","thumbnail_url":"https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-1/FZUiGEaGDbWCiShY8EWNGY_4xnX2ZUSJ7bhqw9h_KAjbxW53bzckvR7YWZq4juTSDB4kOOMmlNImn1Q3WHWVeA","title":"PHP: array_diff - Manual","url":"https://www.php.net/manual/en/function.array-diff.php"}]}}
